--- parity notes (web source: features/admin/components/EndpointSidebar.tsx) ---
* Web component receives endpoints/selected/onSelect as props from ApiPlaygroundPage, which fetches + parses
  /system/openapi (10-row skeleton while loading, PageContainer error on failure). The loading/content/empty/
  error/stale/offline envelope is therefore REAL end-to-end, so the surface is modelled as a shared-layer feed
  (Source -> ViewModel -> UiState) exactly like the sibling HttpStatusTool / ClientUtilitiesSection surfaces --
  not invented (no drift). View performs no HTTP (ADR-002); host injects the concrete /system/openapi source.
* Search box (translation_playground_search) filters on path/summary/operationId (lower-cased contains) ==
  web `filtered` memo. Group-by-tag in first-encounter order, blank tag -> "Other" == web `grouped` memo.
  Per-group defaultOpen = selected.tag == tag || groupCount <= 5 == web rule. All unit-tested off-device.
* MethodBadge (exported in web) reproduced: GET->status.success, POST->chart.speed, PUT->status.warning,
  DELETE->status.danger, PATCH->chart.power; w-12 mono bold 9sp pill with /.20 wash. Selected row -> left
  accent bar (primary) + /.10 wash == web `border-l-2 border-cyan-400 !bg-white/[0.07]`.
* Count line `{matchCount} endpoints` (translation_playground_endpoints); search-empty / data-empty both render
  the friendly "No matching endpoints" (translation_playground_noResults), never a blank box == web behaviour.
* i18n: every visible string resolves through P1/S10 (translation_playground_*, translation_common_refresh,
  translation_a11y_loading); QueryError copy is the shared component's own. No hardcoded English in shipped code.
* a11y: search field exposes a set-text action; group toggles are Role.Button with readable tag+count; each
  endpoint row carries a "VERB /path[, summary]" contentDescription + selected state; refresh + retry are named.
* Telemetry: stateful EndpointSidebar emits view.opened {surface: "EndpointSidebar"} once via the P1/S11 Logger.

